# cp — caps.decl
#
# Wave: R50
# Doc:  design/tooling/r49-r50-plan.md §5.6 in the paideia-os repo.
#
# cp copies a source file to a destination. Its M1 milestone (design +
# skeleton + argv + first-runnable single-file `cp a b`) declares the
# BASELINE cap set every invocation receives from the loader's InitCap
# sidecar (paideia-os src/kernel/core/loader/init_caps.pdx, R20b.M4).
#
# The M1 baseline is the minimum for a single-file copy: identity root
# for audit, read authority on the source, write authority on the
# destination-parent subtree, a filesystem transaction cap so the copy
# is atomic (partial write rolls back at the TXN boundary), and the
# IPC pipe substrate for the schema records M3 will emit.
#
# Cross-subtree elevate (KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL) is NOT ambient — M3-003
# adds a per-op elevate request when the destination-parent path
# exceeds the invoker's scope. M1 refuses cross-subtree copies with a
# diagnostic on stderr; the invoker sees a clear message rather than a
# silent cap-narrow.
#
# Format: `requires:` lists cap-kind names + narrowed rights + optional
# scope. The M1 caps-decl reader (shared with every R49/R50 tool at
# libpdx-cap.M2) resolves each name to its KIND_* ordinal at exec time,
# matches the loader-seeded cap set against this list, and fails-fast
# with CAP_MANIFEST_MISSING / CAP_MANIFEST_EXTRA if the two do not agree.
requires:
  # Identity root. The copy asserts destination-user-write authority via
  # a cap-tail check before it opens the destination file (D3 audit-
  # first, upgraded from the R48.M1 KIND_USER = 0x190 substrate at
  # src/kernel/core/cap/kind_user.pdx).
  - KIND_USER (self)

  # Baseline pipe substrate (R20b, base kind 5). M3 wires libpdx-
  # semantic-pipe on top to emit CopyProgressRecord[]; stdin/stdout/
  # stderr endpoints are seeded by shell at exec via InitCap.
  - KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT (invoke)

  # Read authority on the source subtree. Narrowed to READ (no write).
  # The actual source path is a per-invocation argument; the loader
  # narrows the cap tail's subtree to the argument-path prefix at exec.
  # KIND_PDXFS_FILE = 0x195 (R42 substrate, landed in paideia-os commit
  # 411ad0e).
  - KIND_PDXFS_FILE (read, <src>)

  # Write authority on the destination-parent subtree. Same narrowing
  # discipline: the loader restricts the cap tail to the destination-
  # parent path prefix at exec so cp cannot write outside the argument.
  - KIND_PDXFS_FILE (write, <dst-parent>)

  # Filesystem transaction cap. Opened once per `cp` invocation so a
  # per-file failure rolls back every already-written byte. Prevents
  # partial-copy states from becoming visible. KIND_PDXFS_TXN = 0x196
  # (R42 substrate, landed alongside KIND_PDXFS_FILE at commit 411ad0e).
  - KIND_PDXFS_TXN (invoke)

# --- elevate-broker binding (cp.ENH-011) --------------------------------
# M3-003 landed src/elevate.pdx (CpElevate::cp_elevate_try_dst_parent),
# manifest.pdxproj carries libpdx-elevate @ ^0.1 as a hard dep, and
# copy.pdx calls cp_elevate_try_dst_parent on every destination-open
# failure — i.e. cp attempts the broker hop on EVERY invocation, not
# only a hypothetical future cross-subtree path. The M1-era comment
# that used to live here ("the cross-subtree path refuses at the
# dispatch layer") stopped being true at M3-003 and this decl was never
# updated to match, so cp's declared cap set did not cover a hop it
# actually attempts. Uncommented now that libpdx-cap's OK|MISSING|EXTRA
# manifest compare would otherwise reject every cp exec.
- KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL (invoke, svc.elevate-broker)   # 0x191 R48.M7

# Declared output schemas — the semantic-pipe schema records this tool
# emits on its stdout. M1 emits none (single-file copy is silent on
# success, prints on stderr on error). M3 introduces CopyProgressRecord[]
# via libpdx-semantic-pipe.
declares_output_schemas: (none)
